{"name":"Golden Age","hex":"#ceab77","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Golden Age","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The oldest and best of the Classical Ages of Man, when people lived innocent lives of happiness and prosperity.","Any previous period similarly viewed as superior to the present."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Golden_Age"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden Age","blocks":[{"text":"The term Golden Age comes from Greek mythology, particularly the Works and Days of Hesiod, and is part of the description of temporal decline of the state of peoples through five Ages, Gold being the first and the one during which the Golden Race of humanity lived. After the end of the first age was the Silver, then the Bronze, after this the Heroic age, with the fifth and current age being Iron."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/The_Silver_Age_%28fresco_by_Pietro_da_Cortona%29.jpg/330px-The_Silver_Age_%28fresco_by_Pietro_da_Cortona%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Age","wikidata":"Q238526"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/2010_Utopien_arche04.jpg/500px-2010_Utopien_arche04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/2010_Utopien_arche04.jpg/1280px-2010_Utopien_arche04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com